# Agent Chat Surfaces (Common Component)

Any client surface that talks to a chat/agent thread (Agent Home, interviews, ADR/PRD/design-doc
assistants, standups, dev sessions, calendar assistant, etc.) MUST build on the shared hook
`useAgentChatSession` (`src/client/hooks/useAgentChatSession.ts`), which wraps `useChatStream`
(`src/client/hooks/useChatStream.ts`) for the SSE subscription.

Do **not** hand-roll agent interaction with raw `fetch` + `EventSource` + `useEffect` polling.
Reuse the common hook so send/cancel/retry, awaiting-response tracking, preparation state, and
progress/streaming flags stay consistent across every surface.

## Use the hook's contract

- **Options**: `locked`, `beforeSend` / `afterSend`, `sendEndpoint` / `cancelEndpoint`,
  `visibleMessageFilter`, `enablePreparationState`, `initialMessages` / `initialStatus`.
- **Actions**: `send(text, { attachments, model })`, `retryLast()`, `cancel()`.
- **Derived flags** (drive UI, don't recompute): `isInteractionBusy`, `isRunning`, `isSending`,
  `isAwaitingAgentResponse`, `isPreparing`, `hasPreparationError`.
- **Stream state**: `visibleMessages`, `streamingText`, `thinkingText`, `toolProgress`,
  `phaseEvents`, `runHealth`, `progressLabel`.

## Sanctioned exception to the TanStack rule

`react-coding-standards.mdc` says server/async state goes through TanStack Query and to never
`fetch` in effects. Agent chat is the **one sanctioned exception**: SSE streaming plus imperative
send/cancel live inside `useChatStream` / `useAgentChatSession`. Route new agent surfaces through
these hooks instead of `useQuery`/`useMutation` — do not re-implement the transport elsewhere.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — reuse the common hook
const session = useAgentChatSession(threadId, {
  enablePreparationState: true,
  beforeSend: async () => { /* confirm / sync token */ },
});
<button disabled={session.isInteractionBusy} onClick={() => session.send(text)}>Send</button>

// ❌ BAD — bespoke transport per component
const es = new EventSource(`/api/chat/threads/${threadId}/stream`);
await fetch(`/api/chat/threads/${threadId}/messages`, { method: 'POST', ... });
```

If the hook is missing a capability, extend `useAgentChatSession` (add an option) rather than
forking the logic into a component.
